<article class="env-lemma" id="0387">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0387">Lemma <span data-tag="0387">33.7.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. Let $\overline{k}$ be a separable algebraic closure of $k$. Then $X$ is geometrically connected if and only if the base change $X_{\overline{k}}$ is connected. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $X_{\overline{k}}$ is connected. Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. There exists a field extension $\overline{k}'/\overline{k}$ such that $k'$ embeds into $\overline{k}'$ as an extension of $k$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0363" data-tag="0363">33.7.6</a> we see that $X_{\overline{k}'}$ is connected. Since $X_{\overline{k}'} \to X_{k'}$ is surjective we conclude that $X_{k'}$ is connected as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>